HST Office: an inline picture of a .docx stays inline when saved as .rtf.

The .docx import makes a w:drawing inline picture a draw object (GraphicObjectShape) anchored as character. The RTF
export wrote every draw object as a floating \shp in a SHAPE field, so the picture came back anchored at the character
with wrap through: it took no room, lay over the text, and the document got shorter (s037: 9 pictures, 38 cm, about
one and a half pages). An as-character draw object holding a graphic, not rotated or sheared, is now written as an
inline \pict at its shown size (sw/source/filter/ww8/hst/rtfinlinedrawgraphic.cxx); other draw objects as before.

Test: CppunitTest_sw_rtfexport8 testHstInlineDrawPictureStaysInline (an as-character GraphicObjectShape round-trips
as character with the same size).

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); the new files under
sw/source/filter/ww8/hst/ are HST's own work (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary).
